Consider the compounds listed below and answer the question:<br>&nbsp;
<table border="1" cellpadding="1" cellspacing="1"><tbody><tr><td>(A)</td><td><span class="math-tex">\(\mathrm{CH}_{2}=\mathrm{CH}-\mathrm{CHO}\)</span></td></tr><tr><td>(B)</td><td><span class="math-tex">\(\left(\mathrm{CH}_{3}\right)_{2} \mathrm{C}=\mathrm{C} \left(\mathrm{CH}_{3}\right)_{2}\)</span></td></tr><tr><td>(C)</td><td><span class="math-tex">\( \ \mathrm{CH}_{3} \mathrm{CH}=\mathrm{CH}-\mathrm{CH}_{3}\)</span></td></tr><tr><td>(D)</td><td><span class="math-tex">\( \mathrm{CH}_{3} \mathrm{C} \equiv \mathrm{C}-\mathrm{CH}_{2}-\mathrm{CH}_{3}\)</span></td></tr><tr><td>(E)</td><td><span class="math-tex">\( \mathrm{CH}_{3}-\mathrm{CH}=\mathrm{CH}_{2}\)</span></td></tr><tr><td>(F)</td><td><span class="math-tex">\(\mathrm{CH}_{3}-\mathrm{C} \equiv \mathrm{C}-\mathrm{CH}_{3}\)</span></td></tr></tbody></table>The compounds that can give aldehyde(s) upon ozonolysis is/are:
<table border="1" cellpadding="1" cellspacing="1"><tbody><tr><td>1.</td><td>(A), (B), (D), and (F)</td></tr><tr><td>2.</td><td>(A), (C) and (E)</td></tr><tr><td>3.</td><td>(B), (D) and (E)</td></tr><tr><td>4.</td><td>(A) only</td></tr></tbody></table>

Given below are two statements:&nbsp;
<table border="1" cellpadding="1" cellspacing="1"><tbody><tr><td><strong>Statement I:</strong>&nbsp;</td><td>Friedel Crafts&nbsp;acylation of benzene is done using acetic anhydride in the presence of anhydrous AlCl<sub>3.</sub></td></tr><tr><td><span style="white-space:nowrap;"><strong>Statement II:</strong></span></td><td>Friedel Crafts acylation is an example of an electrophilic substitution reaction.</td></tr></tbody></table>
&nbsp;

<table border="1" cellpadding="1" cellspacing="1"><tbody><tr><td>1.&nbsp;</td><td>Only <strong>Statement I </strong>is correct.</td></tr><tr><td>2.&nbsp;</td><td>Only <strong>Statement II </strong>is correct.</td></tr><tr><td>3.&nbsp;</td><td>Both <strong>Statements I </strong>and <strong>II</strong> are correct.</td></tr><tr><td>4.&nbsp;</td><td>Both&nbsp;<strong>Statements I </strong>and <strong>II</strong> are incorrect.</td></tr></tbody></table>
